From 5a14c426e914927cb368c9b554e0aafd0b02fb1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:26:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HostFS: the host's changes reach the guest

Nothing pushes them: the virtio-fs device grants no notification queue,
so a file the Mac drops into the shared folder never appeared in Tracker,
and one it took away never disappeared -- the guest saw the share as it
was when it last read it, and Tracker, which trusts node monitors, never
re-read.

A low-priority thread on the volume now asks, every two seconds, every
directory the VFS holds a vnode for what it contains now. A directory
whose modification time or size moved is listed again (READDIRPLUS where
the host grants it), and what differs from the node table is passed to
the node monitors: new names are looked up and announced
(notify_entry_created, as idle nodes so their next lookup finds them),
names gone are announced (notify_entry_removed; the table learns on the
next lookup), and entries whose size or modification time moved are
announced (notify_stat_changed), which also drops a file's cached pages
through the existing staleness path. The listing's lookups for entries
already in the table are forgotten at once, so the host counts no extra
reference per pass.

The first listing of a directory is the baseline, not the news: what it
holds was there when the volume was mounted, and goes into the table
without a word. A directory the VFS itself has read took its baseline
then, in dir_fetch().

The pass holds no lock while it talks to the host; the directories it
asks and the table entries it diffs against are pinned (pending), and it
stops between any two of them when the volume goes away. "nopoll" as a
mount parameter turns it off; a failed spawn only logs (the old
open-a-directory-to-see behaviour) and the mount still succeeds.

Verified: private_workspace/hostfs-appear.sh -- the Mac drops, changes
and removes files in the share while the guest watches the volume with
node monitors, and private_workspace/hostfs-test.sh still passes.

Prose-Patch: 0081-hostfs-the-host-s-changes-reach-the-guest.patch 28573c1d78ec9db00e03eb19f5afcbe261451722b63cb1b4a15e22e3761cf3e4
